    "description": "An open museum gallery sized around the moving artifacts. A 2.8 m pendulum and its suspended record share a six-metre floor projection and an accessible side readout. Three enlarged double pendulums paint on separate canvases at the far end. A raised hand recorder keeps a ten-second time trace beside a clear west walkway. The Foucault canvas has its own north-east court; secondary laboratory studies sit along the east wall.",
